[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known: one issue, one fix queued. The reports it holds
come from three different problems. Fixing the parser closes only the first.

## What is in it

<SplitCounts />

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. A parser fix does not touch the form hint, and neither explains the one-day shifts.
</Callout>

## The three problems

1. **Parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day first, so their dates come out flipped. Ticket: [#1](https://github.com/dzmudist/megadev-training/issues/1).
2. **`booking-v3` hint says `MM/DD/YYYY`.** People at day-first tenants type what the hint tells them, and the form reads it their way. A different bug: the hint is wrong. Ticket: [#2](https://github.com/dzmudist/megadev-training/issues/2).
3. **One-day shift.** "Only June", "Lisbon got Tuesday, Toronto got Monday". This looks like time zones or daylight saving, not a swapped day and month. Ticket: [#3](https://github.com/dzmudist/megadev-training/issues/3).

## How the desk tells them apart

The cause depends on the tenant: their locale and the booking form they run. It does not depend
on what intake tagged from the reporter's browser; that tag is a guess and is wrong for a share
of the hint reports. The table below groups by tenant and form.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Lessons

- Matching by subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) merged three bugs into one ticket. Compare cause before you merge.
- A count of reports is a count per problem. Say it in each ticket.

